  "summary": "Single-nucleus and cross-organ profiling now resolve matrix-remodelling states in fibrosis, fibroblasts and microglia across species.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the resolution of cell states and the matrix-remodelling programmes they carry, in fibrotic and glial contexts. In human atrial fibrillation, single-nucleus multi-omics identifies fibroblast states, and JMJD1C is proposed as a mediator of TGF-beta-driven fibroblast remodelling. A cross-organ analysis of human and mouse fibrosis RNA-seq data identifies a conserved 25-gene matrix-remodelling core, although gene-level cross-species concordance is weak. The new element is the pairing of single-nucleus resolution with cross-organ and cross-species comparison, and the core remains only weakly concordant between species. Related preprints extend the logic to neural and microglial states: lysosomal MiT/TFE programmes precede and couple to disease-associated microglia reprogramming, and VIP interneurons show the most disrupted synapse programmes in 5xFAD mice. The heart isoform atlas addresses an adjacent question.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
